column1:
1:7|All her carved images will be smashed;
all her prostitute’s wages burned with fire.
I will devastate all her idols,
for she gathered them from a prostitute’s wages,
and to a prostitute’s wages they will return.”|Repeats wages to retain the accusation's circular economy without assuming a particular cult practice.

6:14|You will eat but not be satisfied;
emptiness will remain within you.
You will put things away but not save them;
what you do save I will give to the sword.|Keeps the difficult inward lack and frustrated preservation with concrete sword outcome.

7:2|The faithful have vanished from the land;
no upright person remains among humanity.
All lie in wait for blood;
each hunts his brother with a net.|Preserves sweeping lament, fraternal predation, and blood/net imagery.

7:12|On that day people will come to you
from Assyria and Egypt’s cities,
from Egypt to the River,
from sea to sea and mountain to mountain.|Uses Egypt for Matsor with fortified-cities alternative noted; keeps unnamed River.
